1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,224
My first memory vanished at midnight. Just a blank void where my eighth birthday cake used to burn brightly.

2
00:00:07,524 --> 00:00:16,188
I found a tiny digital receipt stamped inside my own cerebral cortex. Someone had paid to store their grief here.

3
00:00:16,488 --> 00:00:22,992
A strange man's childhood now occupies the sunny corner of my mind where my mother's laughter used to echo.

4
00:00:23,292 --> 00:00:30,756
I tried to evict him. I screamed into my own thoughts, demanding my stolen joy back from the intruder.

5
00:00:31,056 --> 00:00:38,784
His voice whispered back from the dark, explaining that my brain was the only empty space left on the market.

6
00:00:39,084 --> 00:00:46,404
He pays a fortune in borrowed bliss, trading his heavy sorrow for my sunlit afternoon fields of wheat.

7
00:00:46,704 --> 00:00:54,264
Then I checked the property deed registered deep inside my brainstem. My name wasn't listed anywhere on it.

8
00:00:54,564 --> 00:01:01,452
I am not the owner of this skull. I am just the live-in caretaker keeping the lights on for someone else.

9
00:01:01,752 --> 00:01:09,744
Another payment cleared today. My first kiss was deleted, replaced by a stranger's quiet walk in the rain.

10
00:01:10,044 --> 00:01:15,156
The rent is due tomorrow. Who is currently living in your best moments?
